    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p23-q47-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Show that $(1+\\tan\\theta)(1+\\tan(45^\\circ-\\theta))=2$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Identity proved.\n\nUse $\\tan(45^\\circ-\\theta)=\\dfrac{1-\\tan\\theta}{1+\\tan\\theta}$ and simplify.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(1+\\tan\\theta)(1+\\tan(45^\\circ-\\theta))&=(1+\\tan\\theta)\\left(1+\\frac{1-\\tan\\theta}{1+\\tan\\theta}\\right)\\\\(1+\\tan\\theta)(1+\\tan(45^\\circ-\\theta))&=(1+\\tan\\theta)\\frac{1+\\tan\\theta+1-\\tan\\theta}{1+\\tan\\theta}\\\\(1+\\tan\\theta)(1+\\tan(45^\\circ-\\theta))&=(1+\\tan\\theta)\\frac{2}{1+\\tan\\theta}\\\\(1+\\tan\\theta)(1+\\tan(45^\\circ-\\theta))&=2.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      },
      {
        "id": "p23-q47-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Hence, simplify\n$$(1+\\tan1^\\circ)(1+\\tan2^\\circ)\\cdots(1+\\tan45^\\circ).$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2^{23}$.\n\nPair the factors at $k^\\circ$ and $(45-k)^\\circ$ for $k=1,\\ldots,22$; each pair equals 2. The remaining factor is $1+\\tan45^\\circ=2$.",
          "worked": "Pair the factors for $1^\\circ$ and $44^\\circ$, $2^\\circ$ and $43^\\circ$, through $22^\\circ$ and $23^\\circ$. By part (a), each of these 22 pairs equals 2.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\prod_{k=1}^{45}(1+\\tan k^\\circ)&=\\left[\\prod_{k=1}^{22}(1+\\tan k^\\circ)(1+\\tan(45-k)^\\circ)\\right](1+\\tan45^\\circ)\\\\\\prod_{k=1}^{45}(1+\\tan k^\\circ)&=2^{22}\\times2\\\\\\prod_{k=1}^{45}(1+\\tan k^\\circ)&=2^{23}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      }
    ]
  },
